Quinn is licensed under the MIT license or the Apache License, Version 2.0, at
your option (LICENSE-MIT, LICENSE-APACHE).

This fork adds options that reproduce the QUIC wire behaviour of Chromium and
Firefox (see `FingerprintConfig` in quinn-proto). Most of that code is Quinn's
own: it was written to match packet captures of the browsers and the behaviour
their QUIC implementations document in their sources. Comments such as "as
quiche does" or "as neqo does" mark code of this kind.

The parts listed below go further: they translate code of these
implementations or closely follow its structure. They are additionally covered
by the licence of the respective project, whose full text is in the licenses/
directory. The files concerned name their source in a comment.


